From d20eaa0cbc8fa279cc513d62cd2f93d6a4e47567 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex <6953309+isarrider@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:33:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] avcodec/vc1dec: add frame threading support

Decode VC-1 and WMV3 with frame threading:

- Set up the picture pool in init, so that the frame-thread copies
  share the pool of the first thread; the MpegEncContext itself is still
  initialized lazily on the first frame header.
- Add an update_thread_context callback that (re)initializes the
  size-dependent tables and copies the sequence/entry-point state, the
  persistent picture-level state (rounding control, MV range, RESPIC,
  REFDIST), the intensity compensation LUTs and the field MV flags of the
  last field-coded anchor.
- Finish setup right after the picture header, except for software
  decoded field pictures (decoded with doubled line sizes in the shared
  context; the second field header and the field MV flags can still
  change state used by subsequent pictures) and pictures whose slices
  repeat the picture header. Field-coded streams therefore get little
  parallelism for now.
- Report decoding progress per MB row for frame-coded reference
  pictures (trailing the loop filter), and wait for the referenced rows
  in all motion compensation paths, before copying rows of skipped
  pictures and before reading co-located motion for direct mode.
- Unblock waiting threads if a reference picture fails to decode.
- Wait for a picture decoded by another thread to be finished before
  outputting its frame, as error concealment sets decode_error_flags.

The image (sprite) decoders are unchanged.

