From 4db3a2e89c6e75d691e590399fa2c575e2fbc597 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex <6953309+isarrider@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:46:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] avcodec/vc1dec: finish frame thread setup early for field
 B-pictures

Field pictures are decoded with s->linesize, s->uvlinesize and the line
sizes of the current work picture doubled in place, and their second
field header rewrites quarter_sample and MVRANGE. With
ff_mpeg_update_thread_context(), the next thread could copy any of that
mid-decode, so the previous commit had every field picture finish setup
only after decoding, leaving interlaced field-coded streams nearly
serial.

Sync the reference pictures from their MPVPicture pointers, which do not
change during decoding, instead of copying the work pictures and line
sizes, and stop copying state that every picture header sets again
(quarter_sample, mspel, and MVRANGE in Advanced profile). Field
B-pictures then no longer modify anything vc1_update_thread_context()
reads after their picture header, and can finish setup right after it.
Field I/P pictures still finish setup after decoding: their second field
header can update the intensity compensation state, and their field MV
flags are swapped in only at the end.

Also document the frame threading design at the top of vc1dec.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WgE6y4SVchXBTWL3yw2uiB
