From fb0809ccc4ab8975c7d89c202d738a9147327773 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex <6953309+isarrider@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:11:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] avcodec/vc1dec: let field I/P pictures overlap with frame
 threading

Field-coded I/P pictures finished setup only once they were completely
decoded, and reported their progress only as a whole, so that streams
coded as field pictures were decoded nearly serially. Remove what
required that:

- Report the progress of field pictures per MB row, too: the rows of the
  first field, followed by those of the second field. Wait for the row
  in the field that is actually read, for field pictures referencing
  frame pictures and vice versa as well (ff_vc1_ref_progress()).
- Keep the field MV flags of a field I/P picture in a buffer of its own,
  shared by reference with the threads decoding the following field
  B-pictures, instead of in a per-thread buffer that is swapped in after
  decoding and then copied. Such a buffer starts out zeroed instead of
  with the flags of older pictures; the flags of a picture are only read
  for blocks it has written them for.
- Finish setup of field I/P pictures once the header of their second
  field is parsed. Only that header can still change what the following
  pictures inherit, namely the intensity compensation of the reference
  fields.

The next I/P picture can now start when the second field of the
previous one does, and the B-pictures in between overlap with both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WgE6y4SVchXBTWL3yw2uiB
