- * - Before a thread decodes a picture, vc1_update_thread_context() copies
- *   the state its headers build on from the thread that decoded the
- *   previous one: sequence and entry point parameters, the reference
- *   pictures, intensity compensation and the field MV flags of the last
- *   field-coded anchor. This happens once the previous thread has called
- *   ff_thread_finish_setup(), which vc1_decode_frame() does as early as
- *   possible: right after the picture header for most pictures, after the
- *   header of the second field for field-coded I/P pictures, and after
- *   decoding if slices repeat the picture header.
+ * A field-coded I/P picture hands over later, once the header of its second
+ * field is parsed, as that header still changes what later pictures inherit:
  *
- * - Reference pictures report their progress in MB rows as they are
- *   decoded, trailing the loop filters (see vc1_report_decode_progress() in
- *   vc1_block.c). Field-coded pictures report the rows of their first
- *   field, then those of their second field (see ff_vc1_ref_progress()).
+ *   thread 0 │hdr│═══ first field ═══│hdr 2│═══ second field ═══│
+ *                                          │ finish_setup
+ *                                          ▼
+ *   thread 1                               │hdr│══ first field ══│hdr 2│══ ...
  *
- * - Before a block is predicted from a reference picture, the decoding
- *   thread waits until the rows it reads are available, in the field it
- *   reads them from (vc1_await_ref() in vc1_mc.c). The same applies to the
- *   rows copied for skipped pictures and to the co-located motion read by
- *   B-picture direct mode (vc1_block.c).
+ * Three mechanisms make this work:
+ *
+ *   ┌─ 1. State hand-over ───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+ *   │ Before a thread decodes a picture, vc1_update_thread_context()     │
+ *   │ copies what its headers build on from the thread that decoded the  │
+ *   │ previous picture: sequence/entry point parameters, the reference   │
+ *   │ pictures, intensity compensation and the field MV flags of the     │
+ *   │ last field-coded anchor. That happens once the previous thread has │
+ *   │ called ff_thread_finish_setup(); vc1_decode_frame() does so as     │
+ *   │ early as it can (see the table there).                             │
+ *   └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+ *   ┌─ 2. Progress reporting (producer) ─────────────────────────────────┐
+ *   │ A reference picture reports, MB row by MB row, which rows are      │
+ *   │ final: two rows behind the decoding loop, which is how far the     │
+ *   │ loop filters trail (vc1_report_decode_progress() in vc1_block.c).  │
+ *   │ Field-coded pictures report the rows of their first field, then    │
+ *   │ those of their second field (ff_vc1_ref_progress() in vc1.h).      │
+ *   └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+ *   ┌─ 3. Waiting (consumer) ────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+ *   │ Before a block is predicted from a reference picture, the thread   │
+ *   │ waits until the rows it reads are reported, in the field it reads  │
+ *   │ them from (vc1_await_ref() in vc1_mc.c). Skipped pictures wait     │
+ *   │ before copying a row, and B-picture direct mode before reading     │
+ *   │ co-located motion (vc1_block.c).                                   │
+ *   └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
